gue or forgotten impression, or perhaps she recognizes the *sound* but not the *concept* until reminded. Her confusion after the reminder points to a lack of certainty or recall, rather than complete ignorance or full recognition.\n*   D) just learned about it: This is close to B, but her reaction to the memory prompt suggests she might have encountered it recently, even if she can't place it now.\n\nGiven the sequence where she denies knowing it, then questions her memory when confronted with evidence, the most accurate description is that she has some impression or memory that is currently inaccessible or unclear.\n\nAnswer: \boxed{C}
