he water - The sequence of events (child states inability to swim, loud splash, man says "learn," man gives instructions) strongly implies the man forced the child into the water to start the lesson.\n\nThe initial action that precipitates the instruction to learn is the loud splash occurring right after the age inquiry, making D the most plausible interpretation of the man's action based on the sound effects and dialogue context.\n\nAnswer: $\boxed{D}$
