2025-12-24 01:58:17 | INFO | Q676 id=BV11yrkYME4G_00-03-24_00-03-43 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=The user is asking to identify which of the three acids mentioned in the audio (nitric acid, hydrochloric acid, or sulfuric acid) has the strongest acidity, based on the provided PK values.\n\n1.  **Identify the acids and their PK values from the audio:**\n    *   Sulfuric acid ($\text{H}_2\text{SO}_4$): $\text{pK} = -1.3$ (The audio says "硫酸的 $\text{pK}$ 是 $-1.3$")\n    *   Hydrochloric acid ($\text{HCl}$): $\text{pK} = -3$ (The audio says "盐酸是 $-3$")\n    *   Nitric acid ($\text{HNO}_3$): $\text{pK} = -7$ (The audio says "而硝酸是 $-7$")\n\n2.  **Determine the relationship between $\text{pK}$ value and acidity:**\n    *   Acidity is inversely related to the $\text{pK}$ value. A lower (more negative) $\text{pK}$ value indicates a stronger acid.\n\n3.  **Compare the $\text{pK}$ values:**\n    *   Nitric acid: $-7$\n    *   Hydrochloric acid: $-3$\n    *   Sulfuric acid: $-1.3$\n\n4.  **Conclusion:** Since $-7$ is the lowest (most negative) $\text{pK}$ value, nitric acid is the strongest acid among the three mentioned.\n\n5.  **Match with choices:**\n    *   A) sulfurous acid (Not mentioned with a $\text{pK}$ value in the comparison)\n    *   B) sulfuric acid ($\text{pK} = -1.3$)\n    *   C) hydrochloric acid ($\text{pK} = -3$)\n    *   D) nitric acid ($\text{pK} = -7$)\n\nThe strongest acid based on the audio data is nitric acid, which corresponds to choice D.\n\nAnswer: $\boxed{D}$
