cholic, which aligns perfectly with the Aeolian mode (natural minor). Without absolute pitch confirmation, the *character* of the music strongly points towards the Aeolian mode over the Dorian (which has a major sixth) or the Mixolydian (which is major with a lowered seventh) or Locrian (which is highly dissonant and rarely used melodically).\n\nTherefore, based on the characteristic sound of the melody played by the French horn, the **e Aeolian mode** is the most fitting description among the choices provided.\n\nAnswer: $\boxed{D}$
